<article class="env-lemma" id="0CXD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CXD">Lemma <span data-tag="0CXD">10.109.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a local ring. Let $M$ be an $R$-module. Let $d \geq 0$. The equivalent conditions (1) – (4) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0CXC" data-tag="0CXC">10.109.4</a> are also equivalent to </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="(5)"><p>
there exists a resolution $0 \to P_ d \to P_{d - 1} \to \ldots \to P_0 \to M \to 0$ with $P_ i$ free. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0CXC" data-tag="0CXC">10.109.4</a> and Theorem <a href="/tag/0593" data-tag="0593">10.85.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>